      "problem": "Solve the equation $4x = y$ for the variable $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "We need to isolate the variable $x.$ To do this, we treat $y$ as though it were a constant and apply the addition and multiplication principles as usual.\n\nIn this case, we simply divide both sides of the equation by $4\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\t4x &= y \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {4x} {4} &= \\dfrac y 4 \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {{\\cancel{4}}x} {\\cancel{4}} &= \\dfrac y 4 \\[5pt]\n\t\tx &= \\dfrac y4\n\t}\n$$",
